  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe propose a novel evolutionary strategy that combines real-coded genetic algorithm with local refinement and constraint-handling techniques. The central idea is to represent the step function h as a real-valued vector with bounds [0,1] and the global constraint sum(h) = n_points/2. This formulation avoids the direct combinatorial search space of binary values. The algorithm uses three phases:\n\na) Global exploration with genetic operators (crossover and mutation) to discover promising regions\nb) Local refinement using an adaptive quasi-Newton optimizer \nc) Multi-resolution inheritance based on fractional scaling\n\nThis approach addresses the optimization difficulty by:\n- Reducing local optima trapping through wide panmixis\n- Maintaining constraint satisfaction with repair mechanisms\n- Exploiting knowledge transfer across resolutions by preserving basal patterns\n\nThe algorithm specifically targets the known local optima plateau of 0.38085 by introducing systematic avoidance strategies in mutation and population initialization. The trade space between robustness and exploration is managed through adaptive sigma-scaling of standard deviations. We hypothesize that maintaining both integer and fractional pattern motifs (as seen in the given parent solution) contributes significantly to function minimization.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Domain: n_points = 280 (if init provided) or n_points \u2208 {300, 400} for broader search\n- Variables: h[0:n_points] with bounds \u211d, with additional equality constraint \u2211h[i] = n_points/2\n- Objective function: \n$$C = \\arg\\min \\max_k \\left( (1/n_points) \\cdot \\sum_{i} h[i] \\cdot (1-h[i+k \\mod (2 \\cdot n_points-1)])\\right)$$\n- Equivalently: Use `np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\") * (2.0/n_points) * dx_factor = 2.0/n_points`\n\nAdopt dual formulation for convexity in subproblems:\n- Primary objective: minimize the max-correlation\n- Augmented: incorporate indicator terms for constraint violation\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nStep 1: Set dx = 2.0/n_points and feasibility tol = 1e-8\n\nStep 2: Define repair_with_shift(x):\n- Global bounds enforcement: clip(x, 0.0, 1.0)\n- Local bounds: \n  a. Sum adjustment: diff = n_points/2 - sum(x)\n  b. Distribute adjustment to candidates based on discrepancy distance\n  c. Local iterations (5) to resolve hard bounds\n\nStep 3: Implement AdaptiveMexNES crossover:\n- Primed uniform crossover (pr=0.9 favoring phases)\n- Dynamic configuration based on candidate diversity\n\nStep 4: L-BFGS-B local optimizer with:\n- Feasibility restoration (repair_then_optimize)\n- Step size adaptation based on last 10 iterations\n\nStep 5: Multi-resolution knowledge transfer:\n- For n_new = n_old/k (where k\u2208{2/3, 3/4}):\n  - Downscale by factor k\n  - Phase interpolation preserving evolution traits\n  - Repair loss constraints with knowledge extraction\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Initial population generation:\n  a. 10% Latin hypercube sampling (always)\n  b. 20% Geometric interpolation from parent (when available)\n  c. 70% Random walks adapted from surrogates\n\n- Adaptive annealing:\n  temp_cooldown = 10000 iterations\n  perturbation_dist_std = n_points^(1/4) / (2 + pop_size)\n\n- Debug/monitor metrics:\n  - Feasibility rate\n  - Pareto front between correlation and sum\n  - Topology preservation coefficient\n\n- Krylov subspace projection for directions:\n  update_coef = exp(-damping * eigen_gap)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Compute distribution:\n  for dim in range(n_dims):\n    contribute = dim_feature_importance[dim] * time_per_dim\n\n- Wall clock check every 100 evaluations:\n  if elapsed():\n    save_population()\n    current_best_temp = temperature_schedule(pop_iter)\n\n- Fallback mechanism:\n  if generation > 5000:\n    revert_to_init = True\n    reorient_search()\n\n6. Validation and return contract\ndef validate_result(h, seed, n_points):\n  if not np.all([0<=h[i]<=1 for i in range(n_points)]):\n    raise ConstraintViolation\n  sum_val = np.sum(h)\n  if abs(n_points/2 - sum_val) > 1e-5 * n_points:\n    raise ConstraintViolation\n  # Fast fitness check\n  corr = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n  c5 = np.max(corr) * (2.0/n_points)\n  if c5 > 0.5:  # heuristic bound check\n    warnings.warn(\"Suspiciously large C5 detected\")\n\nfinal_score = compute_c5(h)\nreturn h, final_score, n_points",
